# Git Branch Workflow

- Before implementing any new feature or fix, update `dev` and create a dedicated branch from `dev`.
- Never create a working branch from `master` unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Never implement a new feature or fix directly on `dev` or `master`.
- Use a short descriptive branch name such as `feature/upright-layout`.
- Keep `master` for reviewed or explicitly integrated work.
- For fixes and maintenance, prefer a dedicated `fix/...` branch as well.
- Never commit changes automatically. Leave completed changes uncommitted until the user explicitly requests a commit.
- Never merge a working branch into `master` automatically.
- Only commit or merge when the user explicitly requests that specific action.
- Report the branch name and working-tree status when work is ready for review.
